MathQ: scope of the license
===========================

The MIT License in LICENSE covers the code and documentation written by the
MathQ team (Abdullah Baig, Martí Carrasco and Jordi Rigau). It does not cover:

- Files that come from the organizers' starter repository
  (https://github.com/mpous/datathon-UPC-maths-qualcomm-arduino-unoq), which
  keep the terms set by their authors.
- The fonts in tutor/static/fonts/, which are under the SIL Open Font License
  (see the OFL files next to them).
- Model weights and datasets, which are not in this repository. The fine-tuned
  model is published separately for non-commercial research use only, because
  it was trained on data derived from M3Kang (see finetune/MODEL_CARD.md).
